m1plus-mod
==========

The M1+ Music payload (patch/, tools/pod*.py, test/patch.py) is modelled closely on q2-pod, a
coherent firmware mod for the Shanling Q2:

    q2-pod -- https://github.com/DiamondBond/q2-pod
    Copyright (c) 2026 Diamond Bond
    MIT License

The injection mechanism is q2-pod's: a non-PIC payload compiled with clang/ld.lld and appended to
the UI app (demo) through its final unused PT_NULL program header, rewritten into an RWX PT_LOAD;
checked MIPS PIC-prologue hooks replaced with a jump to the payload; $gp-restoring trampolines that
resume the stock function; stock functions reached through absolute-address macros and libc only
through the app's own GOT slots; the Unicorn test harness (test/patch.py); and the iPod-style menu
design and geometry (q2-pod docs/ipod.md). The linker script (patch/link.ld), the offsets header
(patch/offsets.inc) and the build/appender/trampoline logic follow q2-pod's equivalents.

patch/coverflow.c and test/coverflow.py are ports of q2-pod's files of the same names. The depth
renderer (its projection, compositing, brightness and reflection model, after Rockbox PictureFlow),
the texture-ring bookkeeping and the thumbnail-cache design (one worker thread, the free-space
guard, the empty-file "no art" marker, the ART_NEAR window, the .tmp-then-rename write) follow
q2-pod closely, in places line for line; both files carry its copyright notice in their headers.
Everything that talks to the device -- the stock library queries, the art calls, the page, its
320x480 layout and its touch handling -- is written for the M1 Plus.

Cover Flow's artist scope and the Artists list (patch/coverflow.c coverflow_artist, patch/artists.c,
docs/architecture.md) follow q2-pod's "Artist Albums in Coverflow" (its patch/coverflow.c
coverflow_artist and patch/navigation.c artist list): the ARTIST_ALBUMS scope with the library's
list put back on close, no saved album in the scope, the All albums card only with two albums or
more, and the bounded shelf (coverflow_bounded). The artist list, its albums, the All albums card
(the stock "All songs" row) and the track queries are the M1 Plus's own stock calls; no q2-pod code
is copied verbatim.

The look-theme mod (tools/mod_theme.py, docs/ui.md) follows q2-pod's "Theme: Minimal":
its colours (MINIMAL_CHEVRON, SUDO_MUTED, the neutral pressed grey, the page dots), its pinned
styles/default.bin edits (list fills removed, pressed tint neutral, accent text white), the
settings-disc recolouring rule of its ringnav_image_add and the status glyph set of its
status_icon (redrawn here with Pillow instead of ImageMagick). tools/awtk_style.py reads the theme
format the same way as q2-pod's style_props but was written for this repo.

tools/mod_lists.py (the library list look, docs/ui.md) follows q2-pod's tools/ipod.py
and docs/ipod.md: the choice of pages and dialogs, one pressed colour across lists and dialogs, and the reason it adds no window
animations (q2-pod's note that the lookup-song handlers spin on an animated Back) come from there.
No q2-pod asset is copied.

The iPod-style Now Playing look (tools/mod_nowplaying.py, docs/ui.md) follows q2-pod's
Now Playing design (docs/ipod.md, changelog 1.1.7): its type hierarchy and colour values (NP_TITLE_PX,
NP_META_PX, NP_ARTIST_RGB, NP_ALBUM_RGB, MINIMAL_FILL, SUDO_MUTED, the inactive page-dot grey), the rounded
art, and its "quiet icons" recolouring (tools/ipod.py quiet_icon, redone with PIL). No q2-pod asset
file is copied. The look mods share tools/awtk_style.py (see the look-theme paragraph above).

The boot splash (assets/boot-logo.svg, tools/boot_logo.py, docs/modules/boot.md) adapts q2-pod's
assets/boot-logo.svg and docs/boot.md: its palette and wordmark style; the "M1+" outlines are new
and no q2-pod path is copied. tools/mod_boot.py's jpeg_size is
q2-pod's tools/build.py jpeg_size (the splash frame-header check), and its curly-quote cmap remap
follows q2-pod 1.0.4 (tools/build.py font_quotes), reimplemented without fontTools.

patch/shuffle.c (Shuffle Songs / Albums / Folders, docs/architecture.md) follows q2-pod's Shuffle page
(patch/navigation.c shuffle_play, shuffle_songs, shuffle_groups; patch/playback.c rand_below,
shuffle, make_order): the three actions, Shuffle Songs as the stock Shuffle mode over the library
from a random song, the xorshift32 generator and its seeding, the Fisher-Yates group ranks, the
album and folder orders, the 65,536-song limit and the messages. q2-pod's play-time grouping engine
(its playback hooks) is not ported; the queue is built up front instead.

patch/rows.c, patch/rows.json, tools/mod_ipodrows.py and the stage H demo edits in tools/pod.py
(the library rows, docs/architecture.md) port q2-pod's restyle of the stock list pages: patch/rows.c's
compact_set_row_layout / compact_row_layout follow its patch/navigation.c functions of the same names
closely (the copied default layouter vtable with its layout slot replaced, the text width from the
row's margins and visible siblings, focus-only scrolling, then the stock layout), patch/rows.json
maps its patch/ipod.json immediates and row_layout_calls to this demo with its rule of replacing
only an immediate's 16-bit value, and tools/pod.py's patch_rows follows its tools/ipod.py
patch_code (pinned word, jal to the payload, the rebind resize removed). The constants (pitch, body,
52 px art, inset) follow its docs/ipod.md "Rows"; the M1 values, sites and the list_item body, cover
inset and second-line handling are this repo's. The Shuffle page (stage H) follows q2-pod's Library
Shuffle row and shuffle_menu page. The battery icon (docs/ui.md) follows q2-pod's Icon
battery mode (docs/ipod.md "Battery"); its images are drawn here.

No other q2-pod source file is copied verbatim; the code here was written for the Shanling M1 Plus
with its own addresses, symbols and page set. Files that follow a q2-pod file carry a reference to it in
their header, and q2-pod's copyright is reproduced above as its MIT licence requires.

Fonts (docs/ui.md). tools/mod_font.py builds the UI font from two fonts under the SIL Open
Font License 1.1; their licence texts are in assets/fonts/:

    Inter 4.1 -- https://github.com/rsms/inter
    Copyright (c) 2016 The Inter Project Authors
    SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/OFL-Inter.txt)

    Source Han Sans 2.005R -- https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-han-sans
    Copyright 2014-2025 Adobe (http://www.adobe.com/), with Reserved Font Name 'Source'
    SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/OFL-SourceHanSans.txt)

assets/fonts/Inter-m1plus.ttf is a subset of Inter Medium made by tools/font_inter.py (code points
of Latin, Greek and Cyrillic, tabular digits mapped, hinting and layout tables removed, composites
decomposed, outlines rescaled). Source Han Sans is not redistributed here: the build reads the
pinned release zip that tools/mod_font.py --fetch downloads, and the font it merges into keeps the
stock name (it is not called "Source").

Lucide (docs/ui.md). tools/mod_icons.py renders the icons of Lucide
(https://lucide.dev, lucide-static 1.61.0, tarball SHA-256
62773cd2ee411ad2e37c1973d1e4c4b49f9a6c57da6b5d5d0abca08756ba75f1) into the UI images; the used SVG
sources are in assets/icons/lucide/svg/ and the licence text in assets/icons/lucide/LICENSE:

    Copyright (c) 2026 Lucide Icons and Contributors
    ISC License

Tabler Icons (docs/ui.md). Four glyphs Lucide lacks (brand-tidal, circle-check filled, a-b,
multiplier-1x) come from Tabler Icons 3.49.0 (https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons,
@tabler/icons); the SVG sources are in assets/icons/tabler/svg/ and the licence text in
assets/icons/tabler/LICENSE:

    Copyright (c) 2020-2026 Pawel Kuna
    MIT License

assets/icons/custom/ holds a few icons drawn for this project in the same style.

Wallpaper (docs/ui.md). assets/starry-night-320x480.png is a crop and tone adjustment of
Vincent van Gogh's "The Starry Night" (1889), which is in the public domain (the artist died in 1890;
a faithful reproduction of a flat public-domain work, Wikimedia Commons PD-Art). Source: the Google Art
Project scan, https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Van_Gogh_-_Starry_Night_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg
(1920 px thumbnail, SHA-256 dbca2f16b195f6e83feb98d44c0d98eb0b39f560314efbedfedab9e45caa8a2f);
tools/wallpaper_prepare.py makes it. It replaces the default lock screen picture in the V2.1hB package.
